MathCAT (en rules): no doubled "of" after a large operator, and labeled braces

1. `bigop-both`/`bigop-under` add "of" when something follows the large
   operator. When what follows is an invisible function application
   (U+2061), as after `max_(x∈A)` (max is a function name, so MathCAT
   inserts one before `f(x)`), that operator says "of" itself: the result
   was "the max over x of of f of x". The test now skips U+2061.
2. A rule for the intents `overbrace($content,$label)` and
   `underbrace($content,$label)` that Mathessible gives `⏞(a+b)┴n` /
   `⏟(a+b)┬n` (src/mathessible/mathcat.py, prepare_for_mathcat): "a plus b, with
   brace above, labeled n". Without it the nested movers read "quantity
   quantity a plus b with top brace above with n above".

Applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh on top of upstream 85c89a37. Part 1 is
worth proposing upstream to daisy/MathCAT.

diff --git a/Rules/Languages/en/SharedRules/general.yaml b/Rules/Languages/en/SharedRules/general.yaml
index 832384da..74491460 100644
--- a/Rules/Languages/en/SharedRules/general.yaml
+++ b/Rules/Languages/en/SharedRules/general.yaml
@@ -148,6 +148,22 @@
   - t: "comma"      # phrase(use a 'comma' to divide large numbers or as a decimal point)
   - x: "*[2]"
 
+# Mathessible: a brace over/under an expression with a label (`⏞(a+b)┴n`), given by Mathessible as
+# intent="overbrace($content,$label)": "a plus b, with brace above, labeled n".
+- name: labeled-brace
+  tag: [overbrace, underbrace]
+  match: "count(*)=2"
+  replace:
+  - x: "*[1]"
+  - pause: short
+  - test:
+      if: "self::m:overbrace"
+      then: [t: "with brace above"]
+      else: [t: "with brace below"]
+  - pause: short
+  - t: "labeled"
+  - x: "*[2]"
+
 - name: bigop-both
   tag: large-op
   match: "count(*) = 3"
@@ -162,7 +178,8 @@
   - t: "to"      # phrase(adding 6 'to' 6 equals  12)
   - x: "*[3]"
   - test:
-      if: "following-sibling::*"
+      # Not when an invisible function application follows ("max_(x) f"): it says "of" itself.
+      if: "following-sibling::*[1][not(self::m:mo and .='\u2061')]"
       then: [t: "of"]      # phrase(the square root 'of' 25 equals 5)
 
 - name: bigop-under
@@ -176,7 +193,8 @@
   - t: "over"      # phrase(2 'over' 3 equals two thirds)
   - x: "*[2]"
   - test:
-      if: "following-sibling::*"
+      # Not when an invisible function application follows ("max_(x) f"): it says "of" itself.
+      if: "following-sibling::*[1][not(self::m:mo and .='\u2061')]"
       then: [t: "of"]      # phrase(the square root 'of' 25 equals 5)
 
 - name: largeop
